  "description": "The aesthetic was codified and popularized by Katsuhiro Otomo's landmark manga Akira (1982) and its 1988 anime film adaptation. While heavily influenced by Western cyberpunk works like Blade Runner , Neo-Tokyo reinterpreted the genre to explore distinctly Japanese anxieties surrounding rapid urbanization, corporate power, and the loss of cultural identity in a hyper-technological world.",
